<div style="border: 2px solid #1a5276; padding: 15px; text-align: center; background-color: #e0f2f7;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Learning to Balance – Lesson # 1</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; margin: 5px 0 0 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 1 of 5</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Listening</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Grade:</b> 12th Grade (CEFR: B1.3)</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Scenario:</b> Learning to Balance</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Theme:</b> How to Balance Social and School Activities</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Listening: Interactive: Describe the storyline of an audio or visual narrative. Receptive: Demonstrate comprehension of extended discussions on abstract topics.</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Listening: Can describe the storyline of an audio or visual narrative about balancing school and personal life (e.g., "The speaker shared how they've been balancing their schoolwork with their passion for volunteering.")
            Can comprehend extended discussions on strategies for learning to relax and maintaining well-being (e.g., "The speaker explained that practicing relaxation techniques like deep breathing and time management is essential for mental health.")
            Can ask questions about methods for balancing relaxation with daily responsibilities (e.g., "How does the speaker suggest incorporating relaxation into a busy schedule?" "The speaker says that regular relaxation practices help reduce stress and improve overall well-being.")</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead style="background-color: #f0f8ff;">
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 30%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 20%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification of new vocabulary and key concepts for the lesson. Focus on activating prior knowledge and setting context for the listening task.</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher starts by displaying images of students engaged in various activities: studying intensely, playing sports, using social media, meditating, and looking stressed. Students are asked to briefly discuss in pairs what they see and how these images relate to their own lives. "What `activities` do you see? Which ones do you `prioritize`? Do you ever feel `overwhelming` or `stressed` trying to fit everything in?"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher introduces the theme "How to Balance Social and School Activities" and key vocabulary words on the board (e.g., `balance`, `routine`, `stress`, `relaxation`, `mindfulness`, `prioritize`, `manage`, `unwind`). The teacher models pronunciation, paying specific attention to the short vowel sound /ɪ/ in "activities" (/ækˈtɪvɪtɪz/) and the long vowel sound /iː/ in "relieve" (/rɪˈliːv/). For example, the teacher says: "Balancing school `activities` can help `relieve` `stress`." and has students repeat chorally and individually.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If you `unwind`, are you feeling more or less `stressed`?" (Expected: Less stressed.)</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When we talk about `mindfulness`, are we thinking about the past, the future, or the present moment?" (Expected: The present moment.)</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Learning to Balance". Introduction of an authentic audio input to set the context for listening comprehension.</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> The teacher presents a short (approx. 2-3 minute) audio recording, such as a podcast segment or an interview with a high school student discussing their personal experiences and strategies for `balancing` school and `social life`. The register is informal but reflective. The recording includes examples of the present perfect continuous (e.g., "I `have been studying` late..."), second conditional (e.g., "If I `had` more time..."), and modals of possibility (e.g., "You `might` try...").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Comprehend main ideas and specific details in extended oral texts, specifically narratives about personal experiences.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> Students listen to the audio for the first time.</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Question:</b> "What is the main topic the student in the audio is discussing?" (Write answer on a mini-whiteboard or notebook.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Students listen again and mark statements as True or False based on the audio. (e.g., "The student has been feeling more `stressed` lately because of a heavy `workload`." / "The student believes `downtime` is `unproductive`.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information Matching:</b> Match key phrases heard in the audio with their definitions or related concepts from the new vocabulary list.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Listening. Guided practice using the target grammar structures, vocabulary, and pronunciation heard in the audio.</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will listen for and identify specific grammatical structures (Present Perfect Continuous, Second Conditional, Modals for possibility) and target vocabulary from the audio. They will also practice distinguishing /ɪ/ and /iː/ sounds in context.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice (Listen & Fill-in-the-Blanks):</b> Students receive a transcript excerpt of the audio with blanks for target vocabulary words (e.g., `schedule`, `boundaries`, `flexibility`, `time management`, `procrastination`). They listen to the audio again (segment by segment) and fill in the missing words. Example: "I `have been trying` to create a `flexible` `schedule`."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Practice (Grammar Spotting & Pronunciation Focus):</b> Students listen to specific sentences from the audio and identify:
                            <ul style="list-style-type: circle; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 4px; margin-bottom: 4px;">
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Examples of Present Perfect Continuous: (e.g., "What `have you been doing` to `manage` your `workload`?")</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Examples of Second Conditional: (e.g., "If I `had` more `downtime` after classes, I `would practice` `mindfulness`.")</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Examples of Modals for possibility: (e.g., "You `might need` to `allocate` specific time for `relaxation` to `relieve` `stress`.")</li>
                            </ul>
                            Additionally, they underline words with /ɪ/ and circle words with /iː/ from a provided list of sentences, then listen to verify their choices and pronunciation.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair Interaction (Peer Check & Paraphrasing):</b> In pairs, students compare their answers from the previous activities. They then take turns paraphrasing short sections of the audio to their partner, focusing on using the new vocabulary and the identified grammar structures. For example, "The speaker said she `has been feeling` `overwhelmed`, and if she `could`, she `would improve` her `time management`."</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language heard in a realistic scenario related to "Learning to Balance". Focus on fluency, collaborative interaction, and task completion.</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative Discussion and Advice Giving.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b> Students work in small groups of 3-4. They are given a prompt related to the audio: "Imagine the student from the audio is asking for more advice. Based on what you heard and your own ideas, discuss and suggest ways the student `might` further `improve` their `balance`."</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students take turns describing aspects of the student's `routine` or `stress` points they remember from the audio.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">They then use the target grammar (Present Perfect Continuous, Second Conditional, Modals for possibility) and vocabulary to give suggestions (e.g., "She `has been studying` a lot, so she `should` definitely `plan` `downtime`." "If she `could` `allocate` specific `boundaries` for `social life`, she `might feel` less `overwhelmed`." "I think she `could` incorporate more `mindfulness` to `relieve` `stress`.") and express their opinions (e.g., "I think `flexibility` is key.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Encourage inclusive communication where all group members share their cultural perspectives and contribute strategies for `managing` `stress` effectively, drawing from what they `have been hearing` and discussing.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Each group prepares 2-3 key suggestions to share with the class.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy to check students' comprehension and application of listening skills and target language. Includes student self-assessment.</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist during group discussions and a brief oral summary from each group.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group orally presents their 2-3 key suggestions for the student in the audio. They must clearly describe the storyline (or the student's situation) and offer advice using at least one example of Present Perfect Continuous, one Second Conditional, and one Modal for possibility. The teacher uses a checklist to monitor for accurate use of vocabulary and grammar, pronunciation clarity, and participation.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible pronunciation, especially distinguishing /ɪ/ and /iː/.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of at least 5 target vocabulary words (e.g., `balance`, `stress`, `relaxation`, `schedule`, `prioritize`).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accurate use of Present Perfect Continuous, Second Conditional, and Modals for possibility.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity in describing the storyline or situation from the audio.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Evidence of collaborative interaction within the group.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete the following prompts on a small slip of paper:
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One new strategy for `balancing` activities I learned from the audio or my classmates is..."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I felt confident understanding most of the audio. Yes/No. I need to work on..."</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Student and teacher reflection on the lesson's effectiveness and areas for improvement. Connection to the next lesson in the theme sequence.</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How has this lesson on `balancing` `activities` made you think differently about your own `schedule`?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Which vocabulary word from today do you think is most `effective` for `managing` `stress`?"</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> The listening activities were effective for introducing the core vocabulary and grammar in context. Students were able to grasp the main ideas and some specific details of the audio. The pronunciation practice with /ɪ/ and /iː/ needs continued reinforcement. Some students struggled with the nuance of the Second Conditional; an additional scaffold or example `might` be useful next time. The collaborative task successfully encouraged the use of target language. Adjustments for next lesson: Ensure a quick review of the new vocabulary from this lesson before transitioning to reading to maintain consistency.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In the next lesson (Lesson 2), students will engage in reading comprehension. We will use a text that reinforces the same core vocabulary words (e.g., `balance`, `routine`, `stress`, `relaxation`, `mindfulness`, `prioritize`, `manage`, `unwind`, `schedule`, `boundaries`, `flexibility`, `workload`, `time management`, `downtime`, `procrastination`) and thematic ideas discussed today, allowing them to see these concepts in a written context and deepen their understanding.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">7 min</p></td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>